1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,003
This video records the real Microsoft
Foundry portal for the English lab run.

2
00:00:05,303 --> 00:00:08,146
Personal details and connection addresses
are hidden.

3
00:00:08,446 --> 00:00:13,698
On the project Home page, take the Project
endpoint for your program, not the Azure

4
00:00:13,698 --> 00:00:15,406
OpenAI endpoint beside it.

5
00:00:15,706 --> 00:00:20,173
API-key sign-in is disabled, so the lab
uses your own identity.

6
00:00:21,423 --> 00:00:26,257
Open Models, then Deployments, to see the
four deployments this lab created.

7
00:00:26,557 --> 00:00:32,647
Sol answers the questions, Luna judges the
answers, GPT-5.5 plans the optimization,

8
00:00:32,647 --> 00:00:35,802
and a text embedding model supports
search.

9
00:00:36,102 --> 00:00:38,904
Open the Agent deployment and choose
Details.

10
00:00:39,204 --> 00:00:43,629
Confirm the model version, that
provisioning succeeded, and the limit of

11
00:00:43,629 --> 00:00:45,288
100,000 tokens per minute.

12
00:00:45,588 --> 00:00:49,057
These are this lab's starting limits, not
a universal rule.

13
00:00:49,357 --> 00:00:51,883
Nothing is changed or saved in this
recording.

14
00:00:53,133 --> 00:00:57,773
Under Knowledge, the lab has one knowledge
base that holds eight synthetic policies.

15
00:00:58,073 --> 00:01:01,013
One row in this list is not one policy
document.

16
00:01:01,313 --> 00:01:03,953
Open it to check the planner model and the
source.

17
00:01:04,253 --> 00:01:06,734
Active only means the source is
registered.

18
00:01:07,034 --> 00:01:11,311
You prove retrieval later, through real
answers that call the policy tool.

19
00:01:11,611 --> 00:01:14,676
The free-retrieval banner does not make
the whole lab free.

20
00:01:15,926 --> 00:01:18,486
Open the lab Agent and select version 1.

21
00:01:18,786 --> 00:01:23,776
Its instructions are deliberately plain:
one short sentence, and no calculating

22
00:01:23,776 --> 00:01:24,912
dates or credits.

23
00:01:25,212 --> 00:01:29,065
That leaves visible room for improvement,
which is the point of this lab.

24
00:01:29,365 --> 00:01:33,998
The knowledge base is connected below. Do
not save or publish while you inspect.

25
00:01:35,248 --> 00:01:37,562
Go to Evaluations and choose Create.

26
00:01:37,862 --> 00:01:41,534
Select the Agent and pin version 1, not
the latest version.

27
00:01:41,834 --> 00:01:44,119
Keep Individual turns and One time.

28
00:01:50,511 --> 00:01:55,481
For Data, choose Existing dataset and pick
the registered dev12 for this language.

29
00:01:55,781 --> 00:01:59,218
The preview shows five rows, but the
dataset has twelve.

30
00:01:59,518 --> 00:02:03,817
Do not generate or upload a different
dataset; every run must use the same

31
00:02:03,817 --> 00:02:04,572
twelve rows.

32
00:02:04,872 --> 00:02:09,967
In Configure agents, the user message must
be the item query template, so only the

33
00:02:09,967 --> 00:02:11,707
question reaches the Agent.

34
00:02:12,007 --> 00:02:14,313
Reference answers stay out of the prompt.

35
00:02:15,563 --> 00:02:18,954
The Criteria step needs two evaluators and
one Judge.

36
00:02:19,254 --> 00:02:23,751
The Judge model defaults to the planner
deployment, so change it to your lab judge

37
00:02:23,751 --> 00:02:24,409
deployment.

38
00:02:24,709 --> 00:02:29,606
Clear the recommended evaluators, then add
Relevance and set its threshold to 4.

39
00:02:29,906 --> 00:02:32,108
Relevance is scored from 1 to 5.

40
00:02:32,408 --> 00:02:36,886
Add Task adherence and set its pass value
to 1, because it is binary.

41
00:02:37,186 --> 00:02:40,548
Review selected shows exactly these two
evaluators.

42
00:02:41,048 --> 00:02:46,586
On Review, check the Agent version, scope,
dataset and evaluators, then name the

43
00:02:46,586 --> 00:02:47,417
evaluation.

44
00:02:47,717 --> 00:02:51,888
Submit only once. This video does not
submit a new evaluation.

45
00:02:53,248 --> 00:02:56,080
This is the completed v1 baseline run.

46
00:02:56,380 --> 00:03:00,687
Check that the status is Completed, then
read the Relevance and Task adherence

47
00:03:00,687 --> 00:03:01,184
summary.

48
00:03:01,484 --> 00:03:07,147
In this English run, Relevance passes 10
of 12 and Task adherence passes 11 of 12.

49
00:03:07,447 --> 00:03:10,724
Do not stop at the average. Open a case
and read it.

50
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:16,095
Here the plain v1 declines to apply the
policy to the customer's numbers, so

51
00:03:16,095 --> 00:03:17,162
Relevance is 3.

52
00:03:17,462 --> 00:03:22,109
User view shows the question and the JSON
response, which you compare with the

53
00:03:22,109 --> 00:03:22,586
policy.

54
00:03:23,836 --> 00:03:26,792
Now improve the instructions with Agent
Optimizer.

55
00:03:27,092 --> 00:03:30,278
Open the Agent, choose Optimize, then
Agent.

56
00:03:30,578 --> 00:03:35,306
Select version 1 as the baseline and
choose Instruction only. Turn Model off.

57
00:03:35,606 --> 00:03:39,760
Use the planner deployment as the
optimization model, allow at most two

58
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:43,563
candidates, and use the judge deployment
as the evaluation model.

59
00:03:44,063 --> 00:03:48,731
A run proposes new instruction candidates
and scores each one on your dataset and

60
00:03:48,731 --> 00:03:49,307
criteria.

61
00:03:49,607 --> 00:03:53,923
It tunes instructions only; the model,
tools and data stay fixed.

62
00:03:54,223 --> 00:03:58,003
Next, choose the same registered dataset,
dev12.

63
00:03:58,303 --> 00:04:02,635
For criteria, turn off Custom only to see
the built-in evaluators.

64
00:04:02,935 --> 00:04:05,080
Add Relevance with threshold 4.

65
00:04:05,580 --> 00:04:08,072
Add Task adherence with threshold 1.

66
00:04:08,372 --> 00:04:13,342
The Review step shows an estimated cost.
It is an estimate, not a spending limit.

67
00:04:13,642 --> 00:04:17,917
We close the dialog here, because this job
was already submitted once.

68
00:04:26,455 --> 00:04:29,694
The completed job lists the baseline and
its candidates.

69
00:04:29,994 --> 00:04:35,807
Here the best candidate scores 0.865
against a baseline of 0.844.

70
00:04:36,107 --> 00:04:39,855
That is an internal score, not the managed
evaluation result.

71
00:04:40,155 --> 00:04:43,922
Open View changes to read the candidate
instructions themselves.

72
00:04:44,222 --> 00:04:49,492
The raw candidate copies facts from the
dev12 questions, such as document IDs,

73
00:04:49,492 --> 00:04:51,722
percentages and example answers.

74
00:04:52,022 --> 00:04:55,283
That is memorizing the test, not a general
improvement.

75
00:04:55,583 --> 00:04:59,754
So a person reviews the candidate and
removes those facts before using it.

76
00:05:01,004 --> 00:05:05,303
Version 2 is created from the reviewed
instructions file, not from the raw

77
00:05:05,303 --> 00:05:05,942
candidate.

78
00:05:06,242 --> 00:05:11,190
The review keeps the useful parts: the
output format, using the knowledge base,

79
00:05:11,190 --> 00:05:14,509
routing, and defending against injected
instructions.

80
00:05:14,809 --> 00:05:19,231
It removes the dev12 specifics and
replaces fixed prohibitions with general

81
00:05:19,231 --> 00:05:19,821
guidance.

82
00:05:20,121 --> 00:05:24,406
The model, tools, knowledge connection and
evaluators stay the same.

83
00:05:24,706 --> 00:05:27,153
Promote candidate is not used in this lab.

84
00:05:28,403 --> 00:05:34,428
The evaluation now holds two runs on the
same data, evaluators and Judge: v1 and

85
00:05:34,428 --> 00:05:34,729
v2.

86
00:05:35,029 --> 00:05:39,056
The overall score rises from 88% to 96%.

87
00:05:39,356 --> 00:05:44,386
Select both runs and choose Compare runs,
then set the baseline to the v1 run.

88
00:05:44,686 --> 00:05:48,641
Relevance improves from 3.75 to 4.58.

89
00:05:48,941 --> 00:05:53,303
Task adherence is inconclusive: with
twelve rows, that difference is not

90
00:05:53,303 --> 00:05:54,757
statistically reliable.

91
00:05:55,057 --> 00:05:59,132
Treat this as evidence on twelve
questions, not as production approval.

92
00:05:59,432 --> 00:06:03,532
Both resource groups are still running and
were not deleted. Deleting them is a

93
00:06:03,532 --> 00:06:05,764
separate step that needs explicit
approval.

